  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Drying weather early this week ahead of an unsettled \nweather pattern starting late Wednesday continuing into the weekend.\n\nGOES satellite imagery shows the beginning of clearing skies \nentering western NY while lingering showers move across the eastern \nLake Ontario region. These showers will continue into the north \ncountry this afternoon as the surface low from yesterday's system \ncontinues to slowly progress northeastward through southern Quebec. \nHigh pressure will build into western NY Tuesday promoting drier \nweather through midweek and gradual warming back to near-normal \ntemperatures for early August. \n\nA large scale troughing pattern will move into central Canada \ncentered over the western Hudson Bay by midweek with multiple \nshortwaves passing in the flow across the northern CONUS. This will \nresult in an unsettled weather pattern developing late Wednesday \nwith multiple chances for showers and thunderstorms continuing into \nthe weekend. As the early week high pressure center moves off the \nAtlantic coast Wednesday, southerly flow will begin to return \nmoisture to the area ahead of a cold front that may stall across the \nGreat Lakes region late in the week. At this time, flow appears to \nbe on the weaker side limiting more robust organized convection, but \nPWAT values return towards 1.5-1.7\" that could be supportive of more \nchances for heavy rainfall.",
